This confirms my assessment: the photo set provided is a mismatch for this task. These are exterior façade photos of a large institutional/university building (brick and stone construction, monumental entrance stairs, bike rack sculpture). The only annotated point is a red cross on a plain brick wall in photo 8, but no actual electric meter, meter surroundings context, or main breaker box (open or closed) is depicted anywhere in this set. There is no visible electrical equipment at all — no meter can, no panel door, no breakers.

Given that none of the required subject matter (meter close-up, meter surroundings, panel wall, panel open) is actually observable in these photos, I cannot make confident determinations on any of the four questions. This falls squarely into "photos don't show enough... to judge" for the access questions, and "surroundings too ambiguous" for placement questions, and clearly cannot confirm same-wall relationship.

